  "hypothesis": "Explicit JS feature environments/RNG and asynchronous recursive fill dispatch may alter initializer metadata,counts or child-before-parent behavior.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Feature RNG only follows successful placement; fountain/sink increment after recount; ordinary/theme altar rules and recursive special-room flags follow exact C. Subrooms are visited before own-room early returns and stock dispatch.",
  "observedBehavior": "270 targets (132 feature initializers and138 fill dispatch/flag comparisons) and198 controls (132 no-free-square features and66 all-unfilled trees) match exact compiled C and exported JS. The comparison preserves the upstream fountain/sink double-count quirk and child-before-parent stock-call ordering, including Promise-resolved JS callbacks.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "compiled_oracle",
    "scope": "270 targets (132 feature initializers and138 fill dispatch/flag comparisons) and198 controls (132 no-free-square features and66 all-unfilled trees) match exact compiled C and exported JS. The comparison preserves the upstream fountain/sink double-count quirk and child-before-parent stock-call ordering, including Promise-resolved JS callbacks.",
    "limitations": [
      "Seven keys represent TWO causes: five ordinary-feature environment/RNG delegation keys and two special-room postorder/stock-call dispatch keys. They are not seven independent discoveries.",
      "Feature targets use a regular5\u00d75 OROOM or THEMEROOM,three positions and horizontal bit0/1,with one fountain and sink outside. Fountain draws0..6,altar0..2,sink no feature draw. Controls replace every room square with FOUNTAIN, forcing sampler failure except THEMERoom altar which returns before sampling. Existing source-backed search proofs are reused as dependencies, not recounted as new keys.",
      "The C feature oracle contains exact constructors,search/sampling,terrain setter and full feature recount. Relevant terrain and alignment macros are pinned; Align2amask is copied verbatim. No traps,fluids,invocation square,doors or subrooms occur in feature fixtures. C predicates for absent facilities are explicit adapters. JS production exports execute; only private bydoor is extracted verbatim into the required hook, matching the existing supported component test approach. No full public Lua-binding or generation proof.",
      "Feature comparisons cover terrain,horizontal/altar mask,counts and draw counts/bounds. They preserve the upstream extra fountain/sink increment after recount. They do not prove all geometry,independent RNG,invalid setter behavior,feature interactions or runtime drinking/altar use. Old terrain is ROOM in successful construction; no ice/object/timer behavior is exercised.",
      "Fill comparison covers11 room types,no-fill or flag-only states (ordinary/theme use normal rather than flag-only),one normal-shop state,three rectangular tree shapes up to depth2,and synchronous/Promise-resolved shop hooks. Final9-bit flags and ordered room-index/shop-type/flags-before-call triples agree. All-unfilled controls have neither flags nor calls.",
      "The stock_room boundary is captured in BOTH C and JS. This verifies dispatch/arguments/order only, not the actual stock_room implementation,inventory or actors. Exact source binds the default JS callable to imported stock_room; no claim is made that the capture fixture executes that default. Other population helpers abort if reached. Room construction/storage,orig_rtype,population,RNG inside stocking,Promise rejection,global finalization and runtime are outside scope.",
      "All selected caller and recorded dependency bodies remain unchanged from frozen scan32578f. Original identities/projection and exact current source hashes remain available. Four diagnostic keys,ten changed selection-caller bindings,cave-cap,bottomstairs and three parked gaps are untouched/unresolved. Main-owned repairs and all safety/access exclusions remain separate."
